      "writtenOn": "2018-03-28T07:00:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s less easy to parse when you want to manually generate a changelog between 2 EC versions, and figure out which CLs are relevant, for example.\n\nI prefer going over 50 chars than abbreviating and having to spend 3 more seconds to figure out what the abbreviation means. If you look at the history in the EC codebase, many, many, commits go over 50 chars, we seem to have a soft limit around 60/70 characters\n\nI think Linux kernel, for example, recommends 75 chars:\n\"Possible unwrapped commit description (prefer a maximum 75 chars per line)\"",
      "parentUuid": "0918fa93_ca25f22a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 7
      },
