      "writtenOn": "2018-03-28T23:08:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1 question, 1 remark:\n\n 1. Why 50 chars?\n 2. We all have personal preferences, but when contributing to existing repo, we follow the existing style.\n\n\u003e Anyways, I think chgstv2 isn\u0027t that cryptic and one should be able to tell from context that chgstv2 \u003d\u003d charge_state_v2, especially when the commit only has 1 file diff of charge_state_v2.c...\n\nI often parse git log --oneline to try to figure out what is interesting. I don\u0027t look at the patch itself or what file it changes. When you have 100 commits, it\u0027s easier to parse when commit messages are consistent.",
      "parentUuid": "f617fc01_6b355d43",
